---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { manifest, registry, href } from '../../lib/catalogue';
const publishedSourceIds = new Set(manifest.datasets.flatMap(d => registry.series.find(s => s.id === d.id)?.source_ids ?? []));
const publishedSources = registry.sources.filter(s => publishedSourceIds.has(s.id));
---
<Layout title="Downloads">
  <section class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">DATA / DOWNLOADS</div><h1>Inspect the numbers.<br /><em>Keep the context.</em></h1><p>Published datasets include their units, reference periods, source snapshots and observation statuses.</p></section>
  {manifest.datasets.length === 0 ? <section class="empty-state"><span class="empty-number">0</span><div><h2>No datasets published yet.</h2><p>The source audit is the first milestone. Candidate series contain definitions only; synthetic examples remain in the development workflow.</p><a href={href('series/')}>Browse candidate definitions →</a></div></section> : <section class="series-list">{manifest.datasets.map(d => <article><div><h2>{d.title}</h2><p>{d.coverage.first}–{d.coverage.last} · {d.observation_count} observations</p></div><div><a href={href(`data/${d.files.csv}`)} download>CSV ↓</a> · <a href={href(`data/${d.files.json}`)} download>JSON ↓</a></div></article>)}</section>}
  <section class="details"><h2>Publication manifest</h2><p>The machine-readable manifest lists available files, schema version, coverage, checksums and source terms. Yield observations for 2026 are partial-year averages; government gross debt for 2026 is an IMF forecast.</p><a class="button secondary" href={href('data/manifest.json')} download>Download manifest <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></section>
  {publishedSources.length > 0 && <section class="details"><h2>Data attribution and reuse</h2><p>Data retain their source terms. The combined gross-debt file includes historical data under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0: non-commercial reuse, attribution and sharing under the same terms. The MIT software licence does not apply to these observations.</p>{publishedSources.map(source => <article><h3>{source.title}</h3><p>{source.rights.attribution}</p><p>{source.rights.conditions}</p><a href={source.rights.evidence_url!}>{source.rights.licence} ↗</a></article>)}</section>}
</Layout>
